{# The * wildcard picks a random element, so this page answers differently every run and the
   crawl marks it random rather than comparing it. The values are meant to match the shapes
   noted beside them - 11? is any of 111, 112, 113 and so on.

   The last three lines once asked for a single variable, option or parameter of a named
   level through the dotted group form. That resolves to nothing; only the loop form used
   here works. #}

<br>

{sequence '25..100', name='myRange'/}

{$myRange.*} <br> 
{$*@myRange} <br> 
{$myRange.*@sequence} <br> 

<hr>

{pad name='cool', abc=123, 'fiets', $abc='banaan', $go='nuts', xyz=789, 12*15, 34}

{variables@cool}{$name}={$value} {/variables@cool} <br>
{options@cool}{$name}={$value} {/options@cool} <br>
{parameters@cool}{$value} {/parameters@cool} <br>

{/pad}

<hr>

11?
<br>
{$a.b.1.c.1.*}
<br><br>
11?
<br>
{$a.b.<.c.<.*}
<br><br>
??1
???
??3
<br>
{$a.b.*.c.*.<}
{$a.b.*.c.*.*}
{$a.b.*.c.*.>}
<br><br>
33?
<br>
{$a.b.>.c.>.*}